   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2016, CDC invested $15 million in Ezdehar. In 2017, the European Investment Bank (EIB) also invested $15 million in the fund, which was the first investment in an Egyptian fund since 2011. Other investors include the European Bank for Reconstruction and Development and Dutch DFI FMO, alongside local investors. The fund looks for a typical investment of between $5 million and $15 million.</narrative>
   </description>
